# Sashimi sandbox

The sashimi port (see `docs/sashimi-port-proposal.md`, "Port status" for
acceptance state): the generated data layer (component schemas, the 9
archetype templates plus all live variants, the faction matrix, the wave
script, the Adventure game config), the native simulation core in
`systems/native/systems.c` (26 systems; ordering contract below), and the
playable 60 Hz browser client in `clients/` (architecture below).

Game rules and value provenance: `~/Dev/sashimi/CONTENT-ANALYSIS.md`.

Run headless: `./build/local/test_sashimi_systems` (ctest) includes the
acceptance run — FLECS_SEED pinned + `--config headless-verify` must reach
VICTORY (survive 10800 ticks at 60 Hz).

Run in a browser:

```bash
./tools/build-wasm.sh sashimi           # -> build/wasm-sashimi/
./tools/localhost.sh sashimi --client wasm
# or: cd build/wasm-sashimi && python3 -m http.server 8000
```

## Everything is generated -- edit the generator, not the YAML

`tools/generate_content.py` emits `components/`, `entities/`, `data/` and
`app.yaml` from the sashimi extraction JSON. To regenerate:

```bash
python3 sandboxes/sashimi/tools/generate_content.py \
    [--extraction-dir ~/Dev/sashimi/bin/content-extraction/out] \
    [--sashimi-root ~/Dev/sashimi]
```

- The extraction JSON is produced by the scripts in
  `~/Dev/sashimi/bin/content-extraction/` (venv + unityparser).
- `--sashimi-root` is needed for one asset only:
  `Assets/Data/Spawning/AdventureSpawnConfig.prefab` is re-parsed raw because
  the prefab-tree dump drops the source-prefab default spawn children
  (see "Wave counts" below).
- The generator asserts golden values (slime HP 30, shuriken damage 12,
  victory 180 s, wave totals, ...) so extraction drift fails loudly.

Hand-maintained files: this `CLAUDE.md`, `tools/`, `tests/`,
`systems/native/`.

## Representation decisions

- **Times are seconds, converted by systems.** All durations/cooldowns are
  stored as authored in the Unity assets (seconds). Systems convert with
  `GameTimeConfig.tick_rate` (60 Hz = NetcodeConfig SimulationTickRate).
  `data/waves.yaml` `delay_ticks` is the one tick-denominated field (the
  SpawnDelay enum is already a tick count).
- **Abilities are their hitboxes.** Unity splits an ability across an
  `AbilitySO` + a `ProximityDamageEntity` hitbox variant; here one template
  (e.g. `SlimeAttack`) extends `AbilityBase` -> `ProximityDamageEntity` and
  carries `AbilityConfig` + `AbilityState` + `Collider` + `DamageOnHit`.
- **Classification by component presence, not markers.** `AISteering` =
  AI creature, `Hero` = hero, `Weapon` = weapon child. Marker components are
  reserved for runtime flags (`Defeated`) because `engine_entity_spawn` does
  not auto-copy root-level markers from prefabs.
- **Faction matrix quirk PRESERVED.** `data/faction-matrix.yaml` is a
  verbatim copy of the golden fixture
  `engine/tests/fixtures/faction-matrix-sashimi.yaml`, including the
  HelpEffect_Global one-bit-shift quirk -- golden data matches shipped Unity
  behavior, not documented intent (`engine/tests/test_faction.c` verifies the
  fixture bit-for-bit against the Unity assets).
- **Waves are a data table, not entity templates.** `data/waves.yaml`
  mirrors sashimi's `UnitSpawnWaveElement` buffers: a spawn-director native
  system (slice assembly) reads it like `faction_matrix_load()` reads the
  matrix. 36 waves of `{template, x, y, delay_ticks}` entries do not fit the
  template loader's semantics (templates instantiate all-at-once; waves
  spawn over time), and 509 row-entity prefabs would be pure overhead.
  `WaveState` on the `GameState` entity is the runtime cursor.
- **Wave counts: 509, not CONTENT-ANALYSIS's 502.** The analysis's "502
  entries / Slime 357 / Wolf 41" figures inherited a prefab-tree-dump gap:
  7 spawn entries exist only as prefab-variant modifications of the
  source-default child (`UnitSpawnWaveBase.prefab`'s `SlimeOrange_0`). The
  serialized `_spawns` arrays -- which the Unity baker iterates, and whose
  sizes match the `Wave[N]_i` names the analysis itself trusts -- sum to
  509: Slime 362, Wolf 43, Golem 38, Wisp 38, Cube 28. The generator parses
  the raw prefab for this one asset.
- **`damage_taken_ratio`** (headless-verify profile): a port-added
  GameConfig-style field. Default lives on the GameConfig entity
  (`CombatConfig.damage_taken_ratio: 1.0`); `app.yaml`'s `headless-verify`
  named config sets `0.5` (heroes take 50% damage), selected via
  `--config headless-verify` per root decision 13. The engine's named-config
  parser ignores game-specific keys, so slice assembly must wire the config
  value onto `CombatConfig` at app start; the damage system then consumes
  `CombatConfig.damage_taken_ratio` only.
- **Heart heal is a ratio.** Live sashimi heals 25% of max HP and ignores
  the serialized pickup `Value: 25`; both are kept
  (`PickupConfig.heart_heal_ratio: 0.25` is what the pickup system must use).
- **Hand-placed content**: only the two heroes and the one active gem
  cluster are in `spawn_list`. The SlimePosse "intro" creatures, the placed
  Wolf/Wisp/LargeTealCube, and the lone HealthPickup are inactive in the
  shipped `AdventureEntities.unity` (verified against the scene file --
  CONTENT-ANALYSIS section 11 overstates SlimePosse as active).
- **Skipped on purpose** (CONTENT-ANALYSIS skip list): the 4 legacy weapons
  and weapon pickups, `OldCreatureEntity`, SlimeOrange's unused aura
  variant, thin-client bots, netcode ghost fields, audio/animation SO
  tables (client-side, phase 3), `multiplayerConfig`/`audioConfig`/
  projectile-trail configs.

## System ordering (Unity group -> engine phase mapping)

One engine turn == one 60 Hz tick. The Unity predicted-group pipeline
(`~/Dev/sashimi/SYSTEM-GROUPS.md`) maps onto the engine's five phases
(Init -> Reset -> Move -> Act -> Finalize). Legacy mode runs the exact
`system_order` list in `app.yaml` (slot numbers below); pipeline mode
mirrors it with per-phase DependsOn chains in `systems/native/systems.c`.
Registration covers both modes.

| Slot | System | Unity group (member systems) | Engine phase | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `rewind` | - (engine-level) | Init | history rewind, creates pause |
| 2 | `app_start` | world bootstrap + bake (LocalConnectionManager, subscene load) | Init | once, disables self: FLECS_SEED RNG, faction matrix + waves.yaml load, spatial-hash init, named-config bridge |
| 3 | `game_time` | FirstSimulation `GameTimeSystem_FixedStep` + WorldInit `GameTimeSystem_Predicted` | Init | GameTime.tick++, 0.25 s periodic-clock flag, shared creature level from gems |
| 4 | `hero_ai` | BeginInitialization `ClientGameInputSystem` (headless stand-in) | Init | writes octant-snapped InputDirection to heroes without `PossessedBy`; player clients write InputDirection directly (rt-input.js contract) |
| 5 | `start_of_tick` | (port bookkeeping; Unity clears DamageThisTick inside ResolveDamage) | Reset | removes TookDamage (root decision 8) |
| 6 | `destroy_on_timer` | WorldInit `DestroyGhostOnTimer`/`DestroyEntityAtTick` + FullyPredicted `DestroyGhost` | Reset | timed despawn, children cascade |
| 7 | `ability_machine` | WorldInit `AbilitySystem` + EffectApplication per-ability systems (Slime/Wolf/LargeCubeAttack, LargeCubeCharge) | Reset | data-driven stage machine; AbilityStateChangeSO toggles (locomotion lock, hitbox collider, charge dash) |
| 8 | `weapon_fire` | WorldInit `ProjectileSpawnRequestSystem` | Reset | starts on cooldown; per-level bounce/pierce increments applied at fire time |
| 9 | `spatial_hash` | WorldSim `SpatialHashingSystem` (first in group) | Move | engine spatial.h, cell 0.5, clear+reinsert; rebuilds the shared unit snapshot |
| 10 | `targeting` | WorldSim `EnemyTargetingSystem` (after hash) | Move | acquire radius 5, switch hysteresis 0.15 |
| 11 | `creature_steering` | WorldSim `CreatureMoveDirectionSystem` (before Move) | Move | follow start/stop, flee (Wisp) |
| 12 | `pickup_magnet` | WorldSim `FollowerInputSystem` (before Move) | Move | trigger-radius claim, accel 40 capped at pickup speed |
| 13 | `movement` | WorldSim `MoveSystem` | Move | InputDirection/Velocity * speed * 1/60; StatusSlow multiplier; ArenaBounds clamp; projectiles excluded (slot 21) |
| 14 | `child_offset_sync` | WorldSim `GameplayChildOffsetSyncSystem` (after Move) | Move | parent pos + offset (rotated toward target) |
| 15 | `collision_push` | EffectApplication `CollisionDetection`+`CollisionResponse` (unit-unit path) | Act | own-color separation per faction matrix |
| 16 | `damage_apply` | EffectApplication `CollisionDetection` (trigger path) + `ApplyDamage` + `OnHitEffect` + EffectResolution `ResolveDamage` | Act | faction-filtered; hit-pair reset_time registry; hero i-frames + damage_taken_ratio; StatusEffectOnHit application; periodic auras on the 0.25 s clock |
| 17 | `pickup_collect` | EffectApplication `PickupSystem` | Act | gems -> MatchStats, hearts heal `heart_heal_ratio` of max |
| 18 | `status_effects` | EffectResolution `StatusEffectSystem` | Act | poison damage on the periodic clock; durations per tick; remove on expiry |
| 19 | `defeat` | EffectResolution `DefeatSystem` | Act | HP <= 0 -> Defeated marker |
| 20 | `iframes` | EffectResolution `IFramesSystem` | Act | window countdown |
| 21 | `projectile_lifecycle` | FullyPredicted `ProjectileLifecycleSystem` | Finalize | flight integration, bounce retarget, pierce, spent-spawner, range expiry |
| 22 | `on_defeated` | FullyPredicted `OnDefeatedSystem` (server) | Finalize | drops (gem 50% / heart 3.75%), kills, creature destruction; heroes get RespawnTimer |
| 23 | `respawn` | FullyPredicted `RespawnSystem` | Finalize | full heal + i-frames |
| 24 | `spawn_director` | FullyPredicted `EnemySpawnSystem` (server) | Finalize | WaveState over data/waves.yaml; 5 s between waves |
| 25 | `delayed_spawn` | FullyPredicted `DelayedSpawnSystem` | Finalize | PendingSpawn materialization; creature HP scaled by creature level |
| 26 | `level_up` | FixedStepWorldSimulation `HeroLevelUpSystem` | Finalize | gems vs HeroLevelUp thresholds; full heal; health mult |
| 27 | `app_stop` | BeginInitialization `ServerGameOverSystem` | Finalize | victory 10800 ticks / defeat when all heroes down; end-of-tick check == Unity's start-of-next-tick check |
| 28 | `history_capture` | - (engine-level) | Finalize | snapshot cadence per lean-tick config |

Ordering-sensitive chains (mirroring Unity's intra-group `[UpdateBefore/After]`):

- **input/AI -> movement**: hero_ai(4) writes InputDirection before
  movement(13) integrates it; possession (`PossessedBy`) suppresses AI.
- **hash -> targeting -> steering -> movement -> child sync** (Unity's
  WorldSimulation order, kept verbatim): the hash is built *before*
  movement, exactly as Unity does; damage_apply compensates with a
  broadphase slop (`S_BROADPHASE_SLOP`) covering one tick of motion and
  re-reads live victim positions at narrowphase.
- **collision -> damage -> status -> defeat**: damage_apply(16) precedes
  status_effects(18) and defeat(19), matching
  EffectApplication -> EffectResolution.
- **damage -> projectile lifecycle**: hits recorded by damage_apply this
  tick drive bounce/pierce/spent decisions in projectile_lifecycle(21).
- **defeat -> on_defeated -> respawn**: death consequences and drops run
  once per tick in Finalize (FullyPredicted semantics: every tick is the
  authoritative tick).
- **spawn_director -> delayed_spawn**: wave entries become PendingSpawn
  requests, then materialize after their per-entry delay (1/60 s).
- **weapon/ability ready checks read last tick's unit snapshot** (they run
  in Reset, before this tick's hash rebuild) — the same one-tick staleness
  Unity has, where ProjectileSpawnRequestSystem (WorldInit) precedes
  SpatialHashingSystem (WorldSim); snapshot entries are re-validated
  against the live world because Finalize deletions may have landed.

## Port decisions (values/behaviors not in the extraction)

Documented choices where the Unity content or docs do not pin a value:

- **damage_taken_ratio applies to heroes only** (creatures take full
  damage). Intent per GAMEPLAY.md: ResolveDamage scales by the *attacker's*
  damage multiplier; the ratio is a port-added *victim-side* knob for
  headless verification, defined on `CombatConfig` as a hero
  incoming-damage multiplier (see components/CombatConfig.yaml).
- **I-frames 0.5 s, respawn 5 s, respawn i-frames 2 s**
  (`SASHIMI_IFRAME_TICKS` etc. in systems/native/systems.h): the timers
  exist in Unity (baked disabled) but their durations are not serialized in
  the extraction.
- **LargeCubeCharge dash speed 5 u/s** toward the target locked at windup
  (covers max_range 2.0 within the 0.4 s active window).
- **Bounce resets remaining flight range**; a bounce with no eligible
  target falls back to pierce, else the projectile is spent.
- **Child offsets rotate toward the parent's current target** (offset.x =
  forward), approximating Unity's facing-relative hitboxes.
- **Creatures level from the shared gem count** against the CreatureLevelUp
  table (GAMEPLAY.md: "thresholds level heroes (and creatures) up"):
  damage multiplier at hit time, health multiplier at spawn time.
  `SpawnConfig.spawn_growth` (100) is NOT consumed — its exact Unity
  semantics are unextracted; revisit if creature scaling feels off.
- **`SpawnConfig.spawn_delay`/`spawn_max` not consumed**: all Adventure
  spawns use per-entry `delay_ticks` (VeryShort = 1/60 s) and spawn_max 0
  means unlimited; the global pacing gate has no observable effect on the
  shipped content.
- **Poison damage is unscaled and ignores i-frames/ratio**: it is an
  already-applied effect, not a fresh hit.
- **Unit-unit pushback treats rect colliders as circles** of max half
  extent (narrowphase damage checks use the real shapes).
- **Weapon colliders stay out of the spatial hash**: they are Unity
  target-acquisition triggers (wisp weapon r=25); acquisition here uses
  the projectile's range.
- **Eagle FeatherRecall is structured but deferred**: spent feathers spawn
  `FeatherRecall_Spawner` entities (inert without the recall ability
  system); the recall projectile/haste-buff loop is not in the slice.
- **Spawn warnings / intro telegraph beats** are presentation-only and
  await the client.

## Hero-AI observability contract

`hero_ai` stands in for a human player and may only act on information a
player could observe. Contract as ruled by the user (2026-07-03): **the
whole map is observable** ("map global is ok, all enemies are
observable"), and **efficient retrieval is fine** (global spatial hash,
direct world queries). The constraint is strictly *no future knowledge*:

- **MAY read**: on-field entities anywhere on the map (enemy positions,
  visible collider sizes, alive/defeated state, pickups), own hero state
  (position, speed, HP, level, current input), HUD state (wave number,
  timer, XP/gems, kills), static level geometry (ArenaBounds).
- **MAY remember**: anything previously observed (player memory).
- **MUST NOT read**: the wave script (`g_waves`/`g_wave_entries` from
  `data/waves.yaml`), the spawn director's runtime cursor (`WaveState`:
  next wave, ticks-to-next, spawned totals), pre-spawn requests
  (`PendingSpawn` — an entity counts only once materialized on the
  field), upcoming spawn positions/compositions, RNG state (`rand()`
  seed/sequence, e.g. to predict drops), and un-telegraphed enemy
  internals (`AbilityState`/`WeaponState` cooldown counters, creatures'
  `EnemyTarget`).

No vision radius is imposed: the user ruled whole-map entity reads
observable, so global queries/snapshots ARE the observable set and no
range constant exists (nothing to derive; decision 13 stays untouched).

Audit of every world-state read in the AI-relevant systems
(observable = player-observable; the contract binds `hero_ai` — the
other rows are the game's own mechanics, audited for completeness and
also schedule-blind):

| System | Reads | Classification |
|---|---|---|
| `hero_ai` | own hero Position/MoveSpeed/Health/InputDirection, Defeated, PossessedBy | observable (own state) |
| `hero_ai` | enemies: live query `AISteering+Position+Health` (materialized only), Collider radius | observable (on-field, map-global OK) |
| `hero_ai` | pickups: live query `Pickup+Position` (gem/heart split by `Pickup.effect`) | observable (on-field) |
| `hero_ai` | ArenaBounds (`g_bounds`) wall penalty/clamp | observable (static geometry) |
| `hero_ai` | own-weapon-derived constant `AI_PREF_RANGE` (shuriken range 3.0 - margin) | observable (own kit) |
| `targeting` (creature AI) | unit snapshot (on-field units), own AISteering, CombatConfig hysteresis | on-field only |
| `creature_steering` | own AISteering/EnemyTarget, target's live Position | on-field only |
| `pickup_magnet` | unit snapshot (on-field heroes), own Pickup/Collider/PickupConfig | on-field only |
| `weapon_fire` / `ability_machine` | unit snapshot via `nearest_enemy` (on-field), own cooldowns/config | on-field only (auto-aim is the shipped game's own mechanic) |

**Omniscient reads found: none.** `g_waves`, `WaveState`, `PendingSpawn`
and `rand()` are touched exclusively by `app_start` (load),
`spawn_director`, `delayed_spawn`, and `on_defeated` (drop rolls) — the
simulation side. The AI was already schedule-blind; the contract is
enforced going forward by the comment block at `sashimi_hero_ai` and by
the `pending_spawns_invisible_to_ai` test, which pins the invariant that
`PendingSpawn` request entities carry no Position/AISteering/Health/
Collider/Faction during the delay window (so no AI query, unit snapshot,
or spatial-hash pass can see an enemy before it exists on the field).

## Named-config bridge (headless-verify)

`engine_app_start` records the selected config name on
`engine->active_config`; the sashimi `app_start` system re-parses
`app.yaml`'s `configs:` block for game-specific keys the engine ignores
and writes `damage_taken_ratio` onto the GameConfig entity's
`CombatConfig`. The damage system consumes `CombatConfig.damage_taken_ratio`
only — selecting `--config headless-verify` is the whole switch.

## Runtime-only components (registered natively, not generated)

`TookDamage`, `EnemyTarget`, `WeaponState`, `ProjectileRuntime`,
`HitCount`, `PossessedBy` (player clientId; absence = AI-driven),
`ChargeDash`, `PickupMagnet`, `LocomotionDisabled`, `AbilityInitialized` —
the avk TookDamage pattern: runtime bookkeeping lives in C, the generated
YAML layer stays extraction-faithful.

## Browser client (`clients/`)

Real-time 60 Hz WASM direct-link client on the shared engine runtime
(`engine/clients/lib/` rt-*.js; rt-demo is the reference integration this
replaces the content of). Layout per the root Browser Client Rendering
Policy:

- `clients/wasm/wasm_main.c` -- the bridge (CMake target `sashimi-wasm`,
  relink guard `sashimi_sandbox_stamp`). Steps the engine in-process
  (`wasm_tick` == one 60 Hz turn) and projects state through scalar
  accessors (root decision 19): per renderable root entity
  position/kind/dir/health/max/radius/anim-flags/slot, plus game tick,
  tick rate, victory ticks, wave N + `sashimi_wave_count()`, gems, kills,
  hero level/XP thresholds (HeroLevelUp table), arena bounds,
  game-over/victory/message. Injects nothing but possession + input.
- `clients/wasm/index.html` -- thin DOM shell (canvas + HUD/banner/overlay
  divs) + cwrap transport + one bootstrap call.
- `clients/lib/` -- sandbox client lib: `sashimi-sprites.js` (placeholder
  procedural sheets as rt-sprites manifests -- distinct silhouette per
  kind; real art swaps the painters, the table format and kind mapping
  stay), `sashimi-hud.js` (HP/XP/wave/timer/perf HUD, game-over overlay),
  `sashimi-client.js` (bootstrap wiring RTLoop/RTInput/RTView/RTRender).

Contracts the client depends on:

- **Kinds** -- `wasm_get_unit_kind` values 1..12 (wasm_main.c `SW_KIND_*`)
  are resolved from the spawn prefab (IsA target): HeroEagle 1, HeroFrog 2,
  Slime 3, Wolf 4, Golem 5, Wisp 6, Cube 7, Shuriken 8, Feather 9,
  WispShot 10, Gem 11, Heart 12. `sashimi-sprites.js` KIND_INFO indexes by
  the same values. Kind 0 (weapons, ability children, spawners) is not
  exported.
- **Anim flags** -- bit 0 Defeated, bit 1 TookDamage (this tick), bit 2
  IFramesTimer; the client renders these as alpha/flicker.
- **Join = possession** -- both heroes exist from app start; a device's
  first input claims clientId 1..2 and `wasm_join` sets `PossessedBy`
  {slot} on the first un-possessed hero (hero_ai yields; the client then
  writes InputDirection via `wasm_set_input` -> `sashimi_input_snap`).
  There is no third hero: `wasm_join(3)` returns 0. Local co-op is
  keyboard + gamepad (rt-input.js join flow).
- **Pause is client-side** -- the engine only advances on `wasm_tick`, so
  the client gating the tick call (P key) is a real pause; R re-inits the
  module after game over and re-possesses joined devices.
- **Coordinates** -- the sim is origin-centered (ArenaBounds); the client
  shifts by (-min_x, -min_y) presentation-side. Screen y-down equals sim
  +y; WASD is self-consistent (the arena is vertically mirrored vs Unity's
  y-up view -- presentation-only).

## What slice assembly still needs

- Eagle FeatherRecall ability system (see port decisions above).
- Spawn warnings / intro telegraph beats, real sprite art, audio
  (presentation layer; see the proposal's "Port status" deferred list).

## Tests

- `tests/test_content.c` (ctest: `test_sashimi_content`) validates that
  sandbox select + app start load every template with zero errors and
  spot-checks golden values against CONTENT-ANALYSIS (creature stats,
  weapon kits, poison, level tables, config, faction matrix interactions,
  wave file shape).
- `tests/test_systems.c` (ctest: `test_sashimi_systems`) covers the native
  systems per mechanism (damage ratio math, poison/slow timing, level-up
  application, seeded drop rates, wave schedule, pre-spawn invisibility
  per the hero-AI observability contract, kite-AI keep-range invariant,
  faction-filtered collision, template-inheritance regression)
  and ends with the headless acceptance run: FLECS_SEED=12345 +
  `headless-verify` must reach VICTORY at exactly 10800 ticks.
  `SASHIMI_DEBUG=1` prints per-interval AI/combat traces.

- `tests/test_wasm.js` (ctest `test_wasm_sashimi` in EMSCRIPTEN builds)
  verifies the WASM bridge headless in Node after
  `./tools/build-wasm.sh sashimi`: possession join flow, input control of
  a possessed hero, wave-1 spawns, kind/flag/game-state accessors, engine
  tick-ms stats.

Run from the repo root: `./build/local/test_sashimi_content`,
`./build/local/test_sashimi_systems`,
`node sandboxes/sashimi/tests/test_wasm.js`.
# GENERATED by sandboxes/sashimi/tools/generate_content.py -- do not edit by hand.
# Sashimi data layer (Unity Adventure scene content). Game rules and value
# provenance live in ~/Dev/sashimi/CONTENT-ANALYSIS.md; representation
# decisions in this sandbox's CLAUDE.md.
#
# Adventure GameConfig values (victory 180 s survival, spawn delay 1.25 s,
# 60 Hz tick, 0.25 s periodic tick, drop rates) live on the GameConfig live
# entity (entities/GameConfig.yaml), not here -- the engine app parser has no
# game-specific keys. NOTE for editors -- this file is parsed by a string
# scanner (engine/src/engine/app.c); comments must never contain a section
# key followed by a colon.

name: sashimi
description: "Sashimi survival-action port: data layer (heroes, creatures, waves)"

imports:
  avk:
    components: [MapSize]

# Arena from sashimi's spawn-clamp bounds x [-9.5, 9.5], y [-6.5, 6.5]
# (19 x 13 world units; sashimi positions are continuous floats centered on
# the origin -- see ArenaBounds on the GameConfig entity).
map_size:
  x: 19
  y: 13

# 180 s victory timer at 60 Hz.
max_turns: 10800

# Real-time 60 Hz stepping: lean tick on; unset cadences resolve to
# broadcast on-demand and history off (engine.h lean-tick semantics).
lean_tick: true

configs:
  headless-verify:
    # Headless verification profile: heroes take 50% damage.
    # damage_taken_ratio is a GameConfig-style field (CombatConfig
    # .damage_taken_ratio defaults to 1.0 on the GameConfig entity); per root
    # decision 13 the ratio lives in YAML and is selected via --config. The
    # engine's named-config parser ignores unknown keys, so wiring this value
    # onto CombatConfig at app start is part of slice assembly (documented in
    # CLAUDE.md); the damage system consumes CombatConfig.damage_taken_ratio.
    damage_taken_ratio: 0.5
    lean_tick: true

templates:
  entities: [CreatureEntity, HeroEntity, ProjectileEntity, ProjectileWeaponEntity, ProximityDamageEntity, DamageAuraEntity, StationaryDamageAuraEntity, PickupEntity, AbilityBase, SlimeAttack, WolfAttack, RockGolemAttack, WispAttack, LargeCubeAttack, LargeCubeCharge, CreatureSlimeOrange, CreatureWolf, CreatureRockGolem, CreatureWisp, LargeTealCube, Shuriken_Weapon, Shuriken_Projectile, Feather_Weapon, Feather_Projectile, FeatherRecall_Spawner, FeatherRecall_Projectile, CreatureWisp_Weapon, CreatureWisp_Projectile, HeroFrog, HeroEagle, GemPickup, HeartPickup, DungeonLavaPit, GameConfig, GameState]

# Hand-placed content from Adventure/AdventureEntities.unity: the two heroes
# and the one active gem cluster. The SlimePosse intro creatures, the placed
# Wolf/Wisp/LargeTealCube and the lone HealthPickup are all inactive in the
# shipped scene and are deliberately not spawned.
spawn_list:
  - template: HeroEagle
    params:
      Position: { x: 0.5, y: 0 }
  - template: HeroFrog
    params:
      Position: { x: -0.5, y: 0 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: 0, y: 3.5 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: 0, y: 4 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: 0, y: 4.5 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: -0.5, y: 3.5 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: -0.5, y: 4 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: -0.5, y: 4.5 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: -1, y: 3.5 }
  - template: GemPickup
    params:
      Position: { x: -1, y: 4 }

# Execution order derived from the Unity group pipeline (SYSTEM-GROUPS.md);
# the Unity-group -> engine-phase -> slot mapping table lives in this
# sandbox's CLAUDE.md ("System ordering"). Pipeline mode mirrors this via
# per-phase DependsOn chains in systems/native/systems.c.
system_order:
  - rewind
  - app_start
  - game_time
  - hero_ai
  - start_of_tick
  - destroy_on_timer
  - ability_machine
  - weapon_fire
  - spatial_hash
  - targeting
  - creature_steering
  - pickup_magnet
  - movement
  - child_offset_sync
  - collision_push
  - damage_apply
  - pickup_collect
  - status_effects
  - defeat
  - iframes
  - projectile_lifecycle
  - on_defeated
  - respawn
  - spawn_director
  - delayed_spawn
  - level_up
  - app_stop
  - history_capture
/**
 * SashimiClient — bootstrap for the sashimi real-time WASM client.
 *
 * Wires the shared engine client runtime (lib/rt-*.js from
 * engine/clients/lib/) to the sashimi WASM bridge:
 *
 *   rAF frame (RTLoop, display rate)
 *     ├── accumulator >= 16.67ms?  (fixed 60Hz, spiral guard)
 *     │     ├── RTInput.sample() -> wasm_set_input (octant snap engine-side)
 *     │     ├── wasm_tick()      -> one sashimi simulation tick
 *     │     └── RTView.update(reader)  scalar accessors -> view units
 *     │           (reader.extra copies kind/flags/radius per unit)
 *     └── RTRender.frame(units, alpha)  camera follows P1's hero,
 *           tilemap arena, y-sort, per-kind placeholder sprites, HUD
 *
 * Join = possession: both heroes exist from app start; a device's first
 * input claims clientId 1..2 and wasm_join adds PossessedBy so hero_ai
 * hands the hero over. P pauses (the engine only advances when we call
 * wasm_tick, so a client-side gate is a real pause). R restarts after
 * game over. No game parameter lives here (root CLAUDE.md decision 13) —
 * arena bounds, timers, XP tables, waves all come from the engine.
 */
var SashimiClient = (function() {
    var FLAG_DEFEATED = 1, FLAG_HIT = 2, FLAG_IFRAMES = 4;

    function start(M, opts) {
        var CONFIG = opts.config || 'default';
        var hud = SashimiHUD.init({
            hud: opts.hud, banner: opts.banner, overlay: opts.overlay,
        });

        /* ── Transport: WASM exports via cwrap (scalar accessors) ── */
        var engine = {
            init: M.cwrap('wasm_init_with_config', 'number', ['string']),
            tick: M.cwrap('wasm_tick', 'number', []),
            join: M.cwrap('wasm_join', 'number', ['number']),
            setInput: M.cwrap('wasm_set_input', null, ['number', 'number', 'number']),
            playerEntityId: M.cwrap('wasm_player_entity_id', 'number', ['number']),
            count: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_count', 'number', []),
            id: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_entity_id', 'number', ['number']),
            x: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_x', 'number', ['number']),
            y: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_y', 'number', ['number']),
            dirX: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_dir_x', 'number', ['number']),
            dirY: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_dir_y', 'number', ['number']),
            health: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_health', 'number', ['number']),
            maxHealth: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_max_health', 'number', ['number']),
            radius: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_radius', 'number', ['number']),
            kind: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_kind', 'number', ['number']),
            flags: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_flags', 'number', ['number']),
            slot: M.cwrap('wasm_get_unit_slot', 'number', ['number']),
            getTurn: M.cwrap('wasm_get_turn', 'number', []),
            getTickMs: M.cwrap('wasm_get_tick_ms', 'number', []),
            gameTick: M.cwrap('wasm_get_game_tick', 'number', []),
            tickRate: M.cwrap('wasm_get_tick_rate', 'number', []),
            victoryTicks: M.cwrap('wasm_get_victory_ticks', 'number', []),
            wave: M.cwrap('wasm_get_wave', 'number', []),
            waveCount: M.cwrap('wasm_get_wave_count', 'number', []),
            gems: M.cwrap('wasm_get_gems', 'number', []),
            kills: M.cwrap('wasm_get_kills', 'number', []),
            heroLevel: M.cwrap('wasm_get_hero_level', 'number', []),
            nextLevelXp: M.cwrap('wasm_get_next_level_xp', 'number', []),
            levelXp: M.cwrap('wasm_get_level_xp', 'number', []),
            isGameOver: M.cwrap('wasm_is_game_over', 'number', []),
            isVictory: M.cwrap('wasm_is_victory', 'number', []),
            gameOverMessage: M.cwrap('wasm_get_game_over_message', 'string', []),
            arenaMinX: M.cwrap('wasm_get_arena_min_x', 'number', []),
            arenaMinY: M.cwrap('wasm_get_arena_min_y', 'number', []),
            arenaMaxX: M.cwrap('wasm_get_arena_max_x', 'number', []),
            arenaMaxY: M.cwrap('wasm_get_arena_max_y', 'number', []),
        };

        if (!engine.init(CONFIG)) {
            hud.setBanner('engine init failed (config: ' + CONFIG + ')');
            return null;
        }

        /* Arena: sim space is origin-centered (ArenaBounds); the renderer
           works in [0, mapW) x [0, mapH). Shift here, presentation-side. */
        var arena = {
            minX: engine.arenaMinX(), minY: engine.arenaMinY(),
            maxX: engine.arenaMaxX(), maxY: engine.arenaMaxY(),
        };
        var mapW = arena.maxX - arena.minX;
        var mapH = arena.maxY - arena.minY;

        /* ── Reader: scalar accessors -> RTView, arena-shifted ── */
        var reader = {
            count: engine.count,
            id: engine.id,
            x: function(i) { return engine.x(i) - arena.minX; },
            y: function(i) { return engine.y(i) - arena.minY; },
            dirX: engine.dirX,
            dirY: engine.dirY,
            health: engine.health,
            maxHealth: engine.maxHealth,
            slot: engine.slot,
            extra: function(u, i) {
                u.kind = engine.kind(i);
                u.flags = engine.flags(i);
                u.radius = engine.radius(i);
            },
        };

        /* ── Shared runtime ── */
        var sprites = SashimiSprites.build();
        var view = RTView.init();
        var input = RTInput.init({
            maxPlayers: 2,   /* two heroes exist: co-op = possession */
            onJoin: function(clientId, label) {
                var eid = engine.join(clientId);
                hud.setBanner(eid
                    ? label + ' joined as P' + clientId +
                      ' — second device joins on its first input.  P: pause'
                    : label + ': no free hero to possess');
            },
        });
        var render = RTRender.init({
            canvas: opts.canvas,
            mapW: mapW, mapH: mapH,
            tilePx: 64,
            followRate: 5,
            unitDefs: sprites.defs,
            defFor: function(u) { return sprites.defName(u.kind); },
            sizeFor: function(u, tilePx) {
                return tilePx * sprites.size(u.kind);
            },
            stateFor: function(u) {
                if (u.flags & FLAG_DEFEATED) return 'idle';
                return u.moving ? 'walk' : 'idle';
            },
            alphaFor: function(u, t) {
                if (u.flags & FLAG_DEFEATED) return 0.3;
                if (u.flags & FLAG_IFRAMES)
                    return 0.45 + 0.35 * Math.sin(t * 24);
                if (u.flags & FLAG_HIT) return 0.65;
                return 1;
            },
        });

        var units = [];
        var engineMs = 0;
        var paused = false;
        var gameOverShown = false;

        function freeze() {
            for (var i = 0; i < units.length; i++) {
                units[i].prevX = units[i].x;
                units[i].prevY = units[i].y;
            }
        }

        function firstHero() {
            var p1 = view.find(engine.playerEntityId(1));
            if (p1) return p1;
            for (var i = 0; i < units.length; i++) {
                if (units[i].kind === 1 || units[i].kind === 2)
                    return units[i];
            }
            return null;
        }

        function showGameOver() {
            gameOverShown = true;
            hud.showGameOver({
                victory: engine.isVictory() === 1,
                message: engine.gameOverMessage(),
                timeSec: engine.gameTick() / engine.tickRate(),
                wave: engine.wave(),
                waveCount: engine.waveCount(),
                level: engine.heroLevel(),
                gems: engine.gems(),
                kills: engine.kills(),
            });
        }

        function restart() {
            if (!engine.init(CONFIG)) {
                hud.setBanner('engine re-init failed');
                return;
            }
            view = RTView.init();
            units = [];
            gameOverShown = false;
            paused = false;
            hud.hideGameOver();
            /* Re-possess heroes for already-joined devices. */
            var players = input.players();
            for (var i = 0; i < players.length; i++)
                engine.join(players[i].clientId);
        }

        document.addEventListener('keydown', function(e) {
            if (e.code === 'KeyP' && !engine.isGameOver()) paused = !paused;
            if (e.code === 'KeyR' && engine.isGameOver()) restart();
        });

        var loop = RTLoop.init({
            tickHz: 60,
            maxCatchUp: 5,
            tick: function() {
                if (engine.isGameOver()) {
                    if (!gameOverShown) showGameOver();
                    freeze();
                    return;
                }
                if (paused) { freeze(); return; }
                /* Input is sampled once per simulation tick, never per
                   frame (rt-input contract). */
                var frames = input.sample();
                for (var i = 0; i < frames.length; i++) {
                    engine.setInput(frames[i].clientId,
                                    frames[i].x, frames[i].y);
                }
                engine.tick();
                engineMs = engine.getTickMs();
                units = view.update(reader);
            },
            render: function(alpha, frameDt) {
                render.frame(units, alpha, frameDt, firstHero());
            },
            onStats: function(s) {
                var hero = firstHero();
                var tickRate = engine.tickRate();
                hud.update({
                    hp: hero ? hero.health : 0,
                    maxHp: hero ? hero.maxHealth : 0,
                    down: hero ? (hero.flags & FLAG_DEFEATED) !== 0 : false,
                    level: engine.heroLevel(),
                    gems: engine.gems(),
                    xpFloor: engine.levelXp(),
                    xpNext: engine.nextLevelXp(),
                    wave: engine.wave(),
                    waveCount: engine.waveCount(),
                    timeSec: engine.gameTick() / tickRate,
                    victorySec: engine.victoryTicks() / tickRate,
                    kills: engine.kills(),
                    fps: s.fps,
                    tickMs: s.tickMs,
                    engineMs: engineMs,
                    drawMs: s.renderMs,
                    entities: units.length,
                    players: input.players().map(function(p) {
                        return 'P' + p.clientId;
                    }).join(' '),
                    paused: paused,
                });
            },
            statsEvery: 250,
        });

        loop.start();
        return { loop: loop, engine: engine, restart: restart };
    }

    return { start: start };
})();
/**
 * SashimiHUD — DOM HUD layer for the sashimi client: status panel (HP,
 * XP/level, wave, survival timer, perf counters), join/pause banner, and the
 * game-over / victory overlay. Pure presentation: every number displayed is
 * read from the engine through the WASM bridge.
 */
var SashimiHUD = (function() {
    function pad2(n) { return n < 10 ? '0' + n : '' + n; }
    function mmss(sec) {
        sec = Math.max(0, Math.floor(sec));
        return Math.floor(sec / 60) + ':' + pad2(sec % 60);
    }
    function bar(pct, width) {
        pct = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, pct));
        var full = Math.round(pct * width);
        var out = '';
        for (var i = 0; i < width; i++) out += i < full ? '#' : '.';
        return out;
    }

    function init(els) {
        var hudEl = els.hud, bannerEl = els.banner, overlayEl = els.overlay;

        function update(d) {
            var hpPct = d.maxHp > 0 ? d.hp / d.maxHp : 0;
            var xpSpan = d.xpNext < 0 ? 0 : d.xpNext - d.xpFloor;
            var xpPct = d.xpNext < 0 ? 1
                : (xpSpan > 0 ? (d.gems - d.xpFloor) / xpSpan : 0);
            hudEl.textContent =
                'HP    [' + bar(hpPct, 14) + '] ' +
                    Math.max(0, Math.round(d.hp)) + '/' + Math.round(d.maxHp) +
                    (d.down ? '  DOWN' : '') +
                '\nLV ' + d.level + ' [' + bar(xpPct, 14) + '] ' +
                    (d.xpNext < 0 ? 'MAX' : d.gems + '/' + d.xpNext + ' gems') +
                '\nwave  ' + d.wave + '/' + d.waveCount +
                '\ntime  ' + mmss(d.timeSec) + ' / ' + mmss(d.victorySec) +
                '\nkills ' + d.kills + '   gems ' + d.gems +
                '\n' +
                '\nfps      ' + d.fps.toFixed(0) +
                '\ntick ms  ' + d.tickMs.toFixed(2) +
                    ' (engine ' + d.engineMs.toFixed(2) + ')' +
                '\ndraw ms  ' + d.drawMs.toFixed(2) +
                '\nentities ' + d.entities +
                '\nplayers  ' + (d.players || 'none') +
                (d.paused ? '\n\n== PAUSED (P to resume) ==' : '');
        }

        function setBanner(text) { bannerEl.textContent = text; }

        function showGameOver(d) {
            overlayEl.innerHTML = '';
            var h1 = document.createElement('div');
            h1.className = 'go-title ' + (d.victory ? 'go-victory' : 'go-defeat');
            h1.textContent = d.victory ? 'VICTORY' : 'DEFEAT';
            var msg = document.createElement('div');
            msg.className = 'go-msg';
            msg.textContent = d.message;
            var stats = document.createElement('div');
            stats.className = 'go-stats';
            stats.textContent =
                'survived  ' + mmss(d.timeSec) +
                '\nwave      ' + d.wave + '/' + d.waveCount +
                '\nlevel     ' + d.level +
                '\ngems      ' + d.gems +
                '\nkills     ' + d.kills;
            var hint = document.createElement('div');
            hint.className = 'go-hint';
            hint.textContent = 'Press R to play again';
            overlayEl.appendChild(h1);
            overlayEl.appendChild(msg);
            overlayEl.appendChild(stats);
            overlayEl.appendChild(hint);
            overlayEl.style.display = 'flex';
        }

        function hideGameOver() { overlayEl.style.display = 'none'; }

        return {
            update: update,
            setBanner: setBanner,
            showGameOver: showGameOver,
            hideGameOver: hideGameOver,
        };
    }

    return { init: init };
})();
/**
 * SashimiSprites — placeholder procedural sprite sheets for the sashimi
 * client, expressed as rt-sprites.js unit definitions (sheet + directional
 * animation table with mirror fallback chains — the UnitAnimationDataSO
 * pattern). Real art is a later swap: replace the painters/sheets, keep the
 * table format and kind mapping.
 *
 * Kinds mirror the WASM bridge enum (wasm_main.c SW_KIND_*):
 *   1 HeroEagle  2 HeroFrog  3 Slime  4 Wolf  5 Golem  6 Wisp  7 Cube
 *   8 Shuriken  9 Feather  10 WispShot  11 Gem  12 Heart
 *
 * All values here are presentation-only (silhouette shapes, colors, on-screen
 * sizes). Game parameters stay engine-side (root CLAUDE.md decision 13).
 */
var SashimiSprites = (function() {
    var DIRS = ['E', 'NE', 'N', 'NW', 'W', 'SW', 'S', 'SE'];

    /* ── Sheet builders ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */

    /* Radially symmetric unit (blobs, orbs, pickups): one authored row,
       every state x direction falls back to it. */
    function makeSimpleUnit(fs, frames, fps, anchorY, painter) {
        var canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
        canvas.width = fs * frames;
        canvas.height = fs;
        var g = canvas.getContext('2d');
        for (var f = 0; f < frames; f++) {
            g.save();
            g.translate(f * fs, 0);
            painter(g, fs, [0, 1], f / frames, true);
            g.restore();
        }
        var table = { idle_S: { row: 0, frames: frames, fps: fps } };
        for (var s = 0; s < 2; s++) {
            var state = s === 0 ? 'walk' : 'idle';
            for (var d = 0; d < DIRS.length; d++) {
                var key = state + '_' + DIRS[d];
                if (!table[key]) table[key] = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
            }
        }
        return { sheet: canvas, frameSize: fs, anchorY: anchorY, table: table };
    }

    /* Directional unit (heroes, wolf, golem, cube): authored walk E/S/N
       (4 frames) + idle S (2 frames), left side mirrors right. */
    function makeDirectionalUnit(fs, anchorY, painter) {
        var rows = [
            { key: 'walk_E', face: [1, 0],  frames: 4, walk: true },
            { key: 'walk_S', face: [0, 1],  frames: 4, walk: true },
            { key: 'walk_N', face: [0, -1], frames: 4, walk: true },
            { key: 'idle_S', face: [0, 1],  frames: 2, walk: false },
        ];
        var canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
        canvas.width = fs * 4;
        canvas.height = fs * rows.length;
        var g = canvas.getContext('2d');

        var table = {};
        for (var r = 0; r < rows.length; r++) {
            var row = rows[r];
            for (var f = 0; f < row.frames; f++) {
                g.save();
                g.translate(f * fs, r * fs);
                var phase = row.walk ? f / row.frames : (f === 0 ? 0 : 0.5);
                painter(g, fs, row.face, phase, row.walk);
                g.restore();
            }
            table[row.key] = { row: r, frames: row.frames,
                               fps: row.walk ? 8 : 2 };
        }
        table.walk_W  = { fallback: 'walk_E', mirror: true };
        table.walk_NE = { fallback: 'walk_E' };
        table.walk_SE = { fallback: 'walk_E' };
        table.walk_NW = { fallback: 'walk_E', mirror: true };
        table.walk_SW = { fallback: 'walk_E', mirror: true };
        table.idle_E  = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        table.idle_N  = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        table.idle_NE = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        table.idle_NW = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        table.idle_W  = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        table.idle_SW = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        table.idle_SE = { fallback: 'idle_S' };
        return { sheet: canvas, frameSize: fs, anchorY: anchorY, table: table };
    }

    function shadow(g, fs, w) {
        g.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,0.25)';
        g.beginPath();
        g.ellipse(fs / 2, fs * 0.85, fs * w, fs * w * 0.35, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        g.fill();
    }

    /* ── Painters (one frame each) ───────────────────────────────────── */

    function paintSlime(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            var squash = Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2);
            shadow(g, fs, 0.24);
            var w = fs * (0.26 + squash * 0.04);
            var h = fs * (0.22 - squash * 0.05);
            var cy = fs * 0.85 - h;
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.ellipse(fs / 2, cy + h * 0.35, w, h, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            g.strokeStyle = pal.outline;
            g.lineWidth = 1;
            g.stroke();
            g.fillStyle = pal.eye;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(fs / 2 - w * 0.35, cy, fs * 0.035, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.arc(fs / 2 + w * 0.35, cy, fs * 0.035, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
        };
    }

    function paintWolf(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase, walk) {
            var swing = walk ? Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) : 0;
            shadow(g, fs, 0.3);
            var cy = fs * 0.66 - Math.abs(swing) * fs * 0.02;
            g.strokeStyle = pal.legs;
            g.lineWidth = Math.max(2, fs * 0.05);
            g.lineCap = 'round';
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(fs * 0.36, cy);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.36 + swing * fs * 0.06, fs * 0.85);
            g.moveTo(fs * 0.62, cy);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.62 - swing * fs * 0.06, fs * 0.85);
            g.stroke();
            /* body along facing axis */
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            if (face[1] === 0) {           /* E: long horizontal body */
                g.ellipse(fs / 2, cy, fs * 0.3, fs * 0.14, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            } else {                       /* N/S: foreshortened */
                g.ellipse(fs / 2, cy, fs * 0.18, fs * 0.2, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            }
            g.fill();
            g.strokeStyle = pal.outline;
            g.lineWidth = 1;
            g.stroke();
            /* head + snout toward facing */
            var hx = fs / 2 + face[0] * fs * 0.3;
            var hy = cy + face[1] * fs * 0.2 - fs * 0.06;
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(hx, hy, fs * 0.11, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            g.stroke();
            g.fillStyle = pal.nose;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(hx + face[0] * fs * 0.09, hy + face[1] * fs * 0.07,
                  fs * 0.04, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            /* ears */
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(hx - fs * 0.06, hy - fs * 0.08);
            g.lineTo(hx - fs * 0.02, hy - fs * 0.17);
            g.lineTo(hx + fs * 0.02, hy - fs * 0.08);
            g.fill();
        };
    }

    function paintGolem(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase, walk) {
            var bob = walk ? Math.abs(Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2)) : 0;
            shadow(g, fs, 0.32);
            var cy = fs * 0.55 - bob * fs * 0.02;
            /* bulky rock torso */
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(fs * 0.24, fs * 0.82);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.2, cy);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.34, cy - fs * 0.22);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.66, cy - fs * 0.22);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.8, cy);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.76, fs * 0.82);
            g.closePath();
            g.fill();
            g.strokeStyle = pal.outline;
            g.lineWidth = 1.5;
            g.stroke();
            /* cracks */
            g.strokeStyle = pal.crack;
            g.lineWidth = 1;
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(fs * 0.42, cy - fs * 0.1);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.5, cy + fs * 0.05);
            g.lineTo(fs * 0.44, fs * 0.72);
            g.stroke();
            /* eyes toward facing */
            g.fillStyle = pal.eye;
            var ex = fs / 2 + face[0] * fs * 0.08;
            var ey = cy - fs * 0.12 + face[1] * fs * 0.04;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(ex - fs * 0.07, ey, fs * 0.03, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.arc(ex + fs * 0.07, ey, fs * 0.03, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
        };
    }

    function paintWisp(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            var hover = Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * fs * 0.04;
            shadow(g, fs, 0.16);
            var cy = fs * 0.45 + hover;
            /* glow */
            g.fillStyle = pal.glow;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(fs / 2, cy, fs * 0.22, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            /* core */
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(fs / 2, cy, fs * 0.13, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            /* wavy tail */
            g.strokeStyle = pal.body;
            g.lineWidth = Math.max(2, fs * 0.05);
            g.lineCap = 'round';
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(fs / 2, cy + fs * 0.12);
            g.quadraticCurveTo(fs / 2 + Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * fs * 0.12,
                               cy + fs * 0.26, fs / 2, fs * 0.8 + hover * 0.5);
            g.stroke();
        };
    }

    function paintCube(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase, walk) {
            var tilt = walk ? Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * 0.12 : 0;
            shadow(g, fs, 0.34);
            g.save();
            g.translate(fs / 2, fs * 0.55);
            g.rotate(tilt);
            var s = fs * 0.3;
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.fillRect(-s, -s, s * 2, s * 2);
            g.strokeStyle = pal.outline;
            g.lineWidth = 2;
            g.strokeRect(-s, -s, s * 2, s * 2);
            g.fillStyle = pal.inner;
            g.fillRect(-s * 0.55, -s * 0.55, s * 1.1, s * 1.1);
            /* eyes toward facing */
            g.fillStyle = pal.eye;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(face[0] * s * 0.3 - s * 0.25, face[1] * s * 0.3 - s * 0.15,
                  fs * 0.035, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.arc(face[0] * s * 0.3 + s * 0.25, face[1] * s * 0.3 - s * 0.15,
                  fs * 0.035, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            g.restore();
        };
    }

    function paintShuriken(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            g.save();
            g.translate(fs / 2, fs / 2);
            g.rotate(phase * Math.PI);   /* spins across frames */
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            for (var i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
                g.rotate(Math.PI / 2);
                g.beginPath();
                g.moveTo(0, 0);
                g.lineTo(fs * 0.1, -fs * 0.12);
                g.lineTo(0, -fs * 0.34);
                g.lineTo(-fs * 0.1, -fs * 0.12);
                g.closePath();
                g.fill();
            }
            g.fillStyle = pal.core;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(0, 0, fs * 0.07, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            g.restore();
        };
    }

    function paintFeather(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            g.save();
            g.translate(fs / 2, fs / 2);
            g.rotate(-0.6 + Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * 0.25);
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.ellipse(0, 0, fs * 0.1, fs * 0.3, 0, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            g.strokeStyle = pal.spine;
            g.lineWidth = 1.5;
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(0, -fs * 0.3);
            g.lineTo(0, fs * 0.34);
            g.stroke();
            g.restore();
        };
    }

    function paintOrb(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            var pulse = 1 + Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * 0.18;
            g.fillStyle = pal.glow;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(fs / 2, fs / 2, fs * 0.2 * pulse, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.arc(fs / 2, fs / 2, fs * 0.11 * pulse, 0, Math.PI * 2);
            g.fill();
        };
    }

    function paintGem(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            var f = Math.floor(phase * 4);
            shadow(g, fs, 0.12);
            var cy = fs * 0.55 + Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * fs * 0.03;
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(fs / 2, cy - fs * 0.22);
            g.lineTo(fs / 2 + fs * 0.15, cy);
            g.lineTo(fs / 2, cy + fs * 0.22);
            g.lineTo(fs / 2 - fs * 0.15, cy);
            g.closePath();
            g.fill();
            g.strokeStyle = pal.edge;
            g.lineWidth = 1;
            g.stroke();
            if (f === 1) {  /* sparkle frame */
                g.strokeStyle = pal.sparkle;
                g.beginPath();
                g.moveTo(fs / 2 - fs * 0.24, cy - fs * 0.2);
                g.lineTo(fs / 2 - fs * 0.16, cy - fs * 0.12);
                g.moveTo(fs / 2 - 0.2 * fs, cy - fs * 0.2);
                g.lineTo(fs / 2 - 0.2 * fs, cy - fs * 0.11);
                g.stroke();
            }
        };
    }

    function paintHeart(pal) {
        return function(g, fs, face, phase) {
            var pulse = 1 + Math.sin(phase * Math.PI * 2) * 0.12;
            shadow(g, fs, 0.12);
            var cy = fs * 0.5;
            var s = fs * 0.2 * pulse;
            g.fillStyle = pal.body;
            g.beginPath();
            g.moveTo(fs / 2, cy + s);
            g.bezierCurveTo(fs / 2 - s * 1.4, cy, fs / 2 - s * 0.8, cy - s * 1.1,
                            fs / 2, cy - s * 0.35);
            g.bezierCurveTo(fs / 2 + s * 0.8, cy - s * 1.1, fs / 2 + s * 1.4, cy,
                            fs / 2, cy + s);
            g.fill();
        };
    }

    /* ── Kind registry ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */

    /* def name, on-screen size in world units (presentation-only). */
    var KIND_INFO = {
        1:  { name: 'eagle',    size: 1.0 },
        2:  { name: 'frog',     size: 1.0 },
        3:  { name: 'slime',    size: 0.7 },
        4:  { name: 'wolf',     size: 0.85 },
        5:  { name: 'golem',    size: 1.15 },
        6:  { name: 'wisp',     size: 0.75 },
        7:  { name: 'cube',     size: 1.1 },
        8:  { name: 'shuriken', size: 0.4 },
        9:  { name: 'feather',  size: 0.4 },
        10: { name: 'wispShot', size: 0.35 },
        11: { name: 'gem',      size: 0.45 },
        12: { name: 'heart',    size: 0.5 },
    };

    function build() {
        var FS = 32;
        var defs = {
            eagle: RTSprites.makePlaceholderUnit({
                frameSize: FS,
                body: '#e8e4d8', head: '#f0d890', nose: '#c87820',
                legs: '#907840', outline: '#403010',
            }),
            frog: RTSprites.makePlaceholderUnit({
                frameSize: FS,
                body: '#48a838', head: '#88d060', nose: '#184818',
                legs: '#286020', outline: '#103008',
            }),
            slime: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 6, 0.85, paintSlime({
                body: '#e08828', outline: '#804810', eye: '#301800' })),
            wolf: makeDirectionalUnit(FS, 0.85, paintWolf({
                body: '#8890a0', legs: '#585c68', nose: '#282830',
                outline: '#303440' })),
            golem: makeDirectionalUnit(FS, 0.85, paintGolem({
                body: '#8a7860', outline: '#403828', crack: '#584c3c',
                eye: '#ffb020' })),
            wisp: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 6, 0.8, paintWisp({
                body: '#70e8d8', glow: 'rgba(80,220,200,0.3)' })),
            cube: makeDirectionalUnit(FS, 0.85, paintCube({
                body: '#28a098', inner: '#40c8c0', outline: '#105850',
                eye: '#083430' })),
            shuriken: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 12, 0.5, paintShuriken({
                body: '#c8ccd8', core: '#606878' })),
            feather: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 8, 0.5, paintFeather({
                body: '#f0f0e8', spine: '#a8a8a0' })),
            wispShot: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 8, 0.5, paintOrb({
                body: '#a0f0e0', glow: 'rgba(80,220,200,0.4)' })),
            gem: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 4, 0.7, paintGem({
                body: '#4890f0', edge: '#1848a0', sparkle: '#d0e8ff' })),
            heart: makeSimpleUnit(FS, 4, 4, 0.7, paintHeart({
                body: '#e03848' })),
        };

        return {
            defs: defs,
            defName: function(kind) {
                var k = KIND_INFO[kind];
                return k ? k.name : 'slime';
            },
            size: function(kind) {
                var k = KIND_INFO[kind];
                return k ? k.size : 0.7;
            },
        };
    }

    return { build: build };
})();
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>sashimi — survival action (60Hz WASM)</title>
<style>
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
html, body { height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #10101c; }
canvas { display: block; }
#hud {
    position: fixed; top: 8px; left: 8px; z-index: 5;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 25, 0.78); border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 6px; padding: 8px 12px;
    color: #9fe8a0; font-family: 'SF Mono', 'Cascadia Code', Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.5; white-space: pre;
}
#banner {
    position: fixed; bottom: 12px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
    z-index: 5; color: #ccc; font-family: monospace; font-size: 13px;
    background: rgba(10, 10, 25, 0.78); border: 1px solid #333;
    border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 14px; white-space: pre;
}
#overlay {
    position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 10; display: none;
    flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    gap: 14px; background: rgba(8, 8, 18, 0.82);
    color: #ddd; font-family: monospace; text-align: center;
}
#overlay .go-title { font-size: 52px; letter-spacing: 8px; font-weight: bold; }
#overlay .go-victory { color: #8fe89a; text-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(90, 230, 120, 0.5); }
#overlay .go-defeat { color: #e86a6a; text-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(230, 80, 80, 0.5); }
#overlay .go-msg { font-size: 13px; color: #999; }
#overlay .go-stats { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; white-space: pre; text-align: left; }
#overlay .go-hint { font-size: 13px; color: #8ab6e8; margin-top: 10px; }
#version { position: fixed; bottom: 2px; right: 6px; color: #444; font: 10px monospace; z-index: 5; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<canvas id="canvas"></canvas>
<div id="hud">loading…</div>
<div id="banner">Press WASD / arrows or move a gamepad stick to join (2-player co-op possession) — P: pause</div>
<div id="overlay"></div>
<div id="version">dev</div>

<!-- Thin client per the Browser Client Rendering Policy: DOM shell +
     WASM-export transport + bootstrap. Loop/render/input/view logic is the
     shared engine runtime (lib/rt-*.js, source: engine/clients/lib/);
     sashimi-specific sprites/HUD/bootstrap live in the sandbox lib
     (lib/sashimi-*.js, source: sandboxes/sashimi/clients/lib/). -->
<script src="flecs-ecs.js"></script>
<script src="lib/rt-loop.js"></script>
<script src="lib/rt-input.js"></script>
<script src="lib/rt-view.js"></script>
<script src="lib/rt-sprites.js"></script>
<script src="lib/rt-render.js"></script>
<script src="lib/sashimi-sprites.js"></script>
<script src="lib/sashimi-hud.js"></script>
<script src="lib/sashimi-client.js"></script>
<script>
FlecsECS().then(function(M) {
    SashimiClient.start(M, {
        config: new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('config') || 'default',
        canvas: document.getElementById('canvas'),
        hud: document.getElementById('hud'),
        banner: document.getElementById('banner'),
        overlay: document.getElementById('overlay'),
    });
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
/*
 * WASM entry point for the sashimi real-time client.
 *
 * Direct-link transport (rt-demo pattern): the browser steps the engine
 * in-process at 60Hz (wasm_tick) and reads state through per-field scalar
 * accessors (root CLAUDE.md decision 19). All game parameters come from the
 * sandbox YAML via the engine (root decision 13) — this bridge only projects
 * simulation state for rendering; it injects nothing but possession + input.
 *
 * Input path: the client samples devices once per simulation tick and calls
 * wasm_set_input(clientId, x, y) with raw vectors; sashimi_input_snap snaps
 * them to 45-degree octants before writing the InputDirection component —
 * the identical path the headless hero AI uses, so player and AI heroes are
 * indistinguishable to the simulation.
 *
 * Join path: wasm_join(clientId) possesses an un-possessed hero (PossessedBy
 * {slot}); hero_ai skips possessed heroes. Both heroes exist from app start
 * (spawn_list), so local co-op is possession, not spawning: P1 takes the
 * first free hero, P2 the second. No third hero exists — join returns 0.
 */
#include <emscripten.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

#include "engine/engine.h"
#include "engine/simulation.h"
#include "engine/app.h"
#include "engine/templates.h"
#include "systems.h"   /* sashimi native: sashimi_input_snap, sashimi_wave_count */

/* ── Component mirror structs (layouts match the generated YAML schemas;
      same natural-alignment rules as systems/native/systems.c) ────────── */

typedef struct { float x, y; } CVec2;            /* Position, Velocity,
                                                    InputDirection */
typedef struct { float current, max; } CHealth;
typedef struct {
    int32_t shape;                /* 0=none 1=circle 2=rect */
    float radius, width, height;
    ecs_bool_t enabled;
} CCollider;
typedef struct { float xp; int32_t level; } CExperience;
typedef struct { int32_t slot; } CPossessedBy;
typedef struct { int64_t tick; } CGameTime;
typedef struct { int32_t gems, kills; } CMatchStats;
typedef struct { int32_t next_wave, ticks_to_next, spawned_total; } CWaveState;
typedef struct { int32_t tick_rate; float periodic_tick_time; } CGameTimeConfig;
typedef struct { float victory_timer_seconds, game_over_delay_seconds; } CGameOverConfig;
typedef struct { float min_x, min_y, max_x, max_y; } CArenaBounds;
typedef struct {
    int32_t max_level;
    int32_t xp[20];
    float damage[20];
    float health[20];
} CLevelTable;                    /* HeroLevelUp */

/* ── Static state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

static Engine *g_engine = NULL;

#define SW_MAX_UNITS   4096
#define SW_MAX_PLAYERS 4

/* Renderable kinds, resolved from the spawn prefab (IsA target). The
 * client's sprite manifest indexes by these values. */
enum {
    SW_KIND_NONE = 0,
    SW_KIND_HERO_EAGLE = 1,
    SW_KIND_HERO_FROG = 2,
    SW_KIND_SLIME = 3,
    SW_KIND_WOLF = 4,
    SW_KIND_GOLEM = 5,
    SW_KIND_WISP = 6,
    SW_KIND_CUBE = 7,
    SW_KIND_SHURIKEN = 8,
    SW_KIND_FEATHER = 9,
    SW_KIND_WISP_SHOT = 10,
    SW_KIND_GEM = 11,
    SW_KIND_HEART = 12,
    SW_KIND_COUNT
};

/* Anim-state flags exported per unit. */
#define SW_FLAG_DEFEATED 1
#define SW_FLAG_HIT      2
#define SW_FLAG_IFRAMES  4

typedef struct {
    float x, y;
    float dir_x, dir_y;           /* InputDirection (heroes) or Velocity */
    float health, max_health;     /* 0 max = no health bar */
    float radius;                 /* collider radius / max half extent */
    int32_t kind;
    int32_t flags;
    int32_t slot;                 /* 0 = AI, 1..4 = player clientId */
    int32_t entity_id;
} SwUnit;

static SwUnit g_units[SW_MAX_UNITS];
static int g_unit_count = 0;
static double g_tick_ms = 0;

static ecs_entity_t g_players[SW_MAX_PLAYERS + 1] = {0}; /* index by clientId */

/* Prefab entity -> kind mapping, resolved once per init. */
static ecs_entity_t g_kind_prefab[SW_KIND_COUNT] = {0};

/* Cached component/entity ids. */
static struct {
    ecs_entity_t position, velocity, input_direction, health, collider;
    ecs_entity_t hero, experience, possessed_by, defeated, took_damage,
                 iframes_timer;
    ecs_entity_t game_time, match_stats, wave_state;
    ecs_entity_t game_time_config, game_over_config, arena_bounds,
                 hero_level_up;
    ecs_entity_t game_config_e, game_state_e;
} g_ids;

static void resolve_ids(void) {
    ecs_world_t *w = g_engine->world;
#define L(field, name) g_ids.field = ecs_lookup(w, name)
    L(position, "Position");             L(velocity, "Velocity");
    L(input_direction, "InputDirection"); L(health, "Health");
    L(collider, "Collider");             L(hero, "Hero");
    L(experience, "Experience");         L(possessed_by, "PossessedBy");
    L(defeated, "Defeated");             L(took_damage, "TookDamage");
    L(iframes_timer, "IFramesTimer");    L(game_time, "GameTime");
    L(match_stats, "MatchStats");        L(wave_state, "WaveState");
    L(game_time_config, "GameTimeConfig");
    L(game_over_config, "GameOverConfig");
    L(arena_bounds, "ArenaBounds");      L(hero_level_up, "HeroLevelUp");
#undef L
    g_ids.game_config_e = ecs_lookup(w, "GameConfig");
    g_ids.game_state_e = ecs_lookup(w, "GameState");

    static const struct { int kind; const char *tmpl; } KINDS[] = {
        { SW_KIND_HERO_EAGLE, "HeroEagle" },
        { SW_KIND_HERO_FROG,  "HeroFrog" },
        { SW_KIND_SLIME,      "CreatureSlimeOrange" },
        { SW_KIND_WOLF,       "CreatureWolf" },
        { SW_KIND_GOLEM,      "CreatureRockGolem" },
        { SW_KIND_WISP,       "CreatureWisp" },
        { SW_KIND_CUBE,       "LargeTealCube" },
        { SW_KIND_SHURIKEN,   "Shuriken_Projectile" },
        { SW_KIND_FEATHER,    "Feather_Projectile" },
        { SW_KIND_WISP_SHOT,  "CreatureWisp_Projectile" },
        { SW_KIND_GEM,        "GemPickup" },
        { SW_KIND_HEART,      "HeartPickup" },
    };
    memset(g_kind_prefab, 0, sizeof(g_kind_prefab));
    for (size_t i = 0; i < sizeof(KINDS) / sizeof(KINDS[0]); i++)
        g_kind_prefab[KINDS[i].kind] = ecs_lookup(w, KINDS[i].tmpl);
}

static int kind_of(ecs_entity_t e) {
    ecs_entity_t prefab = ecs_get_target(g_engine->world, e, EcsIsA, 0);
    if (!prefab) return SW_KIND_NONE;
    for (int k = 1; k < SW_KIND_COUNT; k++)
        if (g_kind_prefab[k] == prefab) return k;
    return SW_KIND_NONE;
}

/* ── Collection (after each tick) ──────────────────────────────────── */

static void collect_units(void) {
    ecs_world_t *w = g_engine->world;
    g_unit_count = 0;
    if (!g_ids.position) return;

    ecs_query_t *q = ecs_query(w, {
        .terms = {
            { .id = g_ids.position },
            { .id = g_engine->user_entity_tag },
        },
        .cache_kind = EcsQueryCacheNone
    });

    int count = 0;
    ecs_iter_t it = ecs_query_iter(w, q);
    while (ecs_query_next(&it)) {
        for (int i = 0; i < it.count && count < SW_MAX_UNITS; i++) {
            ecs_entity_t e = it.entities[i];
            /* Roots only: weapon/ability children are not renderables. */
            if (ecs_get_target(w, e, EcsChildOf, 0)) continue;

            int kind = kind_of(e);
            if (kind == SW_KIND_NONE) continue;

            SwUnit *u = &g_units[count];
            u->kind = kind;

            const CVec2 *pos = ecs_get_id(w, e, g_ids.position);
            if (!pos) continue;
            u->x = pos->x;
            u->y = pos->y;

            /* Facing source: heroes have InputDirection; creatures,
             * projectiles and pickups move on Velocity. */
            const CVec2 *dir = g_ids.input_direction ?
                ecs_get_id(w, e, g_ids.input_direction) : NULL;
            if (!dir && g_ids.velocity)
                dir = ecs_get_id(w, e, g_ids.velocity);
            u->dir_x = dir ? dir->x : 0.0f;
            u->dir_y = dir ? dir->y : 0.0f;

            const CHealth *hp = g_ids.health ?
                ecs_get_id(w, e, g_ids.health) : NULL;
            u->health = hp ? hp->current : 0.0f;
            u->max_health = hp ? hp->max : 0.0f;

            const CCollider *c = g_ids.collider ?
                ecs_get_id(w, e, g_ids.collider) : NULL;
            u->radius = 0.2f;
            if (c) {
                if (c->shape == 1) u->radius = c->radius;
                else if (c->shape == 2)
                    u->radius = (c->width > c->height ? c->width
                                                      : c->height) * 0.5f;
            }

            u->flags = 0;
            if (g_ids.defeated && ecs_has_id(w, e, g_ids.defeated))
                u->flags |= SW_FLAG_DEFEATED;
            if (g_ids.took_damage && ecs_has_id(w, e, g_ids.took_damage))
                u->flags |= SW_FLAG_HIT;
            if (g_ids.iframes_timer && ecs_has_id(w, e, g_ids.iframes_timer))
                u->flags |= SW_FLAG_IFRAMES;

            const CPossessedBy *pb = g_ids.possessed_by ?
                ecs_get_id(w, e, g_ids.possessed_by) : NULL;
            u->slot = pb ? pb->slot : 0;

            const int32_t *eid = ecs_get_id(w, e, g_engine->entity_id_comp);
            u->entity_id = eid ? *eid : 0;

            count++;
        }
    }
    ecs_query_fini(q);
    g_unit_count = count;
}

/* ── Lifecycle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_init_with_config(const char *config_name) {
    if (g_engine) engine_fini(g_engine);
    memset(g_players, 0, sizeof(g_players));
    g_unit_count = 0;
    g_tick_ms = 0;

    g_engine = engine_init(NULL);
    if (!g_engine) return 0;

    if (!engine_sandbox_select(g_engine, "sashimi")) {
        engine_fini(g_engine);
        g_engine = NULL;
        return 0;
    }

    /* Empty / "default" mean the app.yaml top-level values. */
    const char *cfg = (config_name && config_name[0] &&
                       strcmp(config_name, "default") != 0) ? config_name
                                                            : NULL;
    AppStartResult asr;
    if (!engine_app_start(g_engine, cfg, &asr)) {
        engine_fini(g_engine);
        g_engine = NULL;
        return 0;
    }

    resolve_ids();
    collect_units();
    return 1;
}

/* Advance exactly one 60Hz simulation tick (lean mode: pipeline only). */
EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_tick(void) {
    if (!g_engine) return -1;
    double t0 = emscripten_get_now();
    TurnResult tr;
    if (engine_sim_turn(g_engine, &tr)) {
        engine_turn_result_free(&tr);
    }
    collect_units();
    g_tick_ms = emscripten_get_now() - t0;
    return g_engine->turn_counter;
}

/* ── Input / join flow ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* Possess an un-possessed hero for player clientId (1..4). Idempotent —
 * returns the already-possessed hero's entity_id if this client joined
 * before. Returns 0 when no free hero exists (2 heroes -> 2 players). */
EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_join(int client_id) {
    if (!g_engine || client_id < 1 || client_id > SW_MAX_PLAYERS) return 0;
    ecs_world_t *w = g_engine->world;

    if (g_players[client_id] && ecs_is_alive(w, g_players[client_id])) {
        const int32_t *eid = ecs_get_id(w, g_players[client_id],
                                        g_engine->entity_id_comp);
        return eid ? *eid : 0;
    }
    if (!g_ids.hero || !g_ids.possessed_by) return 0;

    /* First un-possessed hero, lowest entity id (deterministic). */
    ecs_entity_t chosen = 0;
    ecs_query_t *q = ecs_query(w, {
        .terms = {{ .id = g_ids.hero }, { .id = g_engine->user_entity_tag }},
        .cache_kind = EcsQueryCacheNone
    });
    ecs_iter_t it = ecs_query_iter(w, q);
    while (ecs_query_next(&it)) {
        for (int i = 0; i < it.count; i++) {
            ecs_entity_t e = it.entities[i];
            if (ecs_has_id(w, e, g_ids.possessed_by)) continue;
            if (!chosen || e < chosen) chosen = e;
        }
    }
    ecs_query_fini(q);
    if (!chosen) return 0;

    CPossessedBy pb = { client_id };
    ecs_set_id(w, chosen, g_ids.possessed_by, sizeof(pb), &pb);
    /* Stop the last AI-written direction from carrying over. */
    if (g_ids.input_direction) {
        CVec2 *dir = ecs_get_mut_id(w, chosen, g_ids.input_direction);
        if (dir) {
            dir->x = 0; dir->y = 0;
            ecs_modified_id(w, chosen, g_ids.input_direction);
        }
    }

    g_players[client_id] = chosen;
    const int32_t *eid = ecs_get_id(w, chosen, g_engine->entity_id_comp);
    return eid ? *eid : 0;
}

/* Write a 45-degree-snapped InputDirection for one player. Called once per
 * simulation tick with the raw device vector (rt-input.js contract). */
EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
void wasm_set_input(int client_id, double x, double y) {
    if (!g_engine || client_id < 1 || client_id > SW_MAX_PLAYERS) return;
    ecs_entity_t e = g_players[client_id];
    if (!e || !ecs_is_alive(g_engine->world, e)) return;

    float sx, sy;
    sashimi_input_snap((float)x, (float)y, &sx, &sy);

    if (!g_ids.input_direction) return;
    CVec2 *dir = ecs_get_mut_id(g_engine->world, e, g_ids.input_direction);
    if (dir) {
        dir->x = sx;
        dir->y = sy;
        ecs_modified_id(g_engine->world, e, g_ids.input_direction);
    }
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_player_entity_id(int client_id) {
    if (!g_engine || client_id < 1 || client_id > SW_MAX_PLAYERS) return 0;
    ecs_entity_t e = g_players[client_id];
    if (!e || !ecs_is_alive(g_engine->world, e)) return 0;
    const int32_t *eid = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, e,
                                    g_engine->entity_id_comp);
    return eid ? *eid : 0;
}

/* ── Per-unit scalar accessors ─────────────────────────────────────── */

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_unit_count(void) { return g_unit_count; }

#define UNIT_ACC(name, type, field, dflt) \
    EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE \
    type wasm_get_unit_##name(int i) { \
        return (i >= 0 && i < g_unit_count) ? g_units[i].field : (dflt); \
    }

UNIT_ACC(entity_id, int, entity_id, 0)
UNIT_ACC(x, double, x, 0)
UNIT_ACC(y, double, y, 0)
UNIT_ACC(dir_x, double, dir_x, 0)
UNIT_ACC(dir_y, double, dir_y, 0)
UNIT_ACC(health, double, health, 0)
UNIT_ACC(max_health, double, max_health, 0)
UNIT_ACC(radius, double, radius, 0)
UNIT_ACC(kind, int, kind, 0)
UNIT_ACC(flags, int, flags, 0)
UNIT_ACC(slot, int, slot, 0)

#undef UNIT_ACC

/* ── Game-state scalar accessors ───────────────────────────────────── */

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_turn(void) { return g_engine ? g_engine->turn_counter : 0; }

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
double wasm_get_tick_ms(void) { return g_tick_ms; }

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
double wasm_get_game_tick(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_state_e || !g_ids.game_time) return 0;
    const CGameTime *gt = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, g_ids.game_state_e,
                                     g_ids.game_time);
    return gt ? (double)gt->tick : 0;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_tick_rate(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_config_e || !g_ids.game_time_config) return 60;
    const CGameTimeConfig *tc = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world,
                                           g_ids.game_config_e,
                                           g_ids.game_time_config);
    return (tc && tc->tick_rate > 0) ? tc->tick_rate : 60;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
double wasm_get_victory_ticks(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_config_e || !g_ids.game_over_config) return 0;
    const CGameOverConfig *go = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world,
                                           g_ids.game_config_e,
                                           g_ids.game_over_config);
    if (!go) return 0;
    return (double)go->victory_timer_seconds * wasm_get_tick_rate();
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_wave(void) {
    /* Waves released so far (WaveState.next_wave - 1). */
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_state_e || !g_ids.wave_state) return 0;
    const CWaveState *ws = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, g_ids.game_state_e,
                                      g_ids.wave_state);
    return ws ? ws->next_wave - 1 : 0;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_wave_count(void) { return sashimi_wave_count(); }

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_gems(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_state_e || !g_ids.match_stats) return 0;
    const CMatchStats *ms = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, g_ids.game_state_e,
                                       g_ids.match_stats);
    return ms ? ms->gems : 0;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_kills(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_state_e || !g_ids.match_stats) return 0;
    const CMatchStats *ms = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, g_ids.game_state_e,
                                       g_ids.match_stats);
    return ms ? ms->kills : 0;
}

/* Heroes share XP/level (MatchStats.gems drives both); read the first. */
static const CExperience *first_hero_xp(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.hero || !g_ids.experience) return NULL;
    const CExperience *xp = NULL;
    ecs_query_t *q = ecs_query(g_engine->world, {
        .terms = {{ .id = g_ids.hero }, { .id = g_ids.experience }},
        .cache_kind = EcsQueryCacheNone
    });
    ecs_iter_t it = ecs_query_iter(g_engine->world, q);
    while (ecs_query_next(&it)) {
        if (it.count > 0 && !xp)
            xp = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, it.entities[0],
                            g_ids.experience);
    }
    ecs_query_fini(q);
    return xp;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_hero_level(void) {
    const CExperience *xp = first_hero_xp();
    return xp ? xp->level : 1;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
double wasm_get_hero_xp(void) {
    const CExperience *xp = first_hero_xp();
    return xp ? xp->xp : 0;
}

/* Gems required for the next hero level (HeroLevelUp table on GameConfig);
 * -1 at max level. */
EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_next_level_xp(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_config_e || !g_ids.hero_level_up) return -1;
    const CLevelTable *t = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, g_ids.game_config_e,
                                      g_ids.hero_level_up);
    if (!t) return -1;
    int lvl = wasm_get_hero_level();
    int maxl = t->max_level < 20 ? t->max_level : 20;
    if (lvl >= maxl) return -1;
    return t->xp[lvl];
}

/* Gems threshold of the current level (progress-bar floor). */
EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_get_level_xp(void) {
    if (!g_engine || !g_ids.game_config_e || !g_ids.hero_level_up) return 0;
    const CLevelTable *t = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, g_ids.game_config_e,
                                      g_ids.hero_level_up);
    if (!t) return 0;
    int lvl = wasm_get_hero_level();
    if (lvl < 1) lvl = 1;
    if (lvl > 20) lvl = 20;
    return t->xp[lvl - 1];
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_is_game_over(void) { return (g_engine && g_engine->game_over) ? 1 : 0; }

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
int wasm_is_victory(void) {
    return (g_engine && g_engine->game_over &&
            strncmp(g_engine->game_over_message, "Victory", 7) == 0) ? 1 : 0;
}

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
const char *wasm_get_game_over_message(void) {
    return g_engine ? g_engine->game_over_message : "";
}

/* Arena bounds (GameConfig ArenaBounds; sim space is origin-centered). */
#define BOUNDS_ACC(name, field, dflt) \
    EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE \
    double wasm_get_arena_##name(void) { \
        if (g_engine && g_ids.game_config_e && g_ids.arena_bounds) { \
            const CArenaBounds *b = ecs_get_id(g_engine->world, \
                g_ids.game_config_e, g_ids.arena_bounds); \
            if (b) return b->field; \
        } \
        return (dflt); \
    }

BOUNDS_ACC(min_x, min_x, -9.5)
BOUNDS_ACC(min_y, min_y, -6.5)
BOUNDS_ACC(max_x, max_x, 9.5)
BOUNDS_ACC(max_y, max_y, 6.5)

#undef BOUNDS_ACC

EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE
void wasm_free(void) {
    if (g_engine) {
        engine_fini(g_engine);
        g_engine = NULL;
    }
}

int main(void) { return 0; }
